From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Noronha Silva <gustavo@noronha.dev.br>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:24:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] venus: submit only the renderer syncs a submission
 filled

vn_queue_submission_count_semaphore counts a signal semaphore as
needing a renderer sync while vn_semaphore_is_sync_fd says so, which
includes a binary semaphore holding a temporary imported sync fd
payload. vn_queue_submission_init_wait_semaphores then runs first, and
waiting a sync fd semaphore restores its permanent payload. A binary
semaphore that one submission both waits and signals (valid: the wait
unsignals it) has therefore been counted with the imported payload, but
reaches vn_queue_submission_init_syncs holding its permanent DEVICE_ONLY
one, which that function correctly skips. The fence then lands in slot
0, slot 1 is never written, and virtgpu_submit dereferences it.

Seen as a SIGSEGV in virtgpu_submit under gfxrecon-replay: its virtual
swapchain forwards an acquire by submitting a transition that waits and
signals the application's acquire semaphore. The core shows sync_count
2, syncs[1] NULL, and the signal semaphore binary, not exportable, and
DEVICE_ONLY.

Set sync_count from what init_syncs actually filled. The skipped
semaphore needs no renderer sync: it stays in the batch's signal list,
since init_signal_semaphores sees the same restored payload, and the
renderer object signals it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_queue.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_queue.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_queue.c
index 057842a524e..73d3fc3ccf4 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_queue.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_queue.c
@@ -1049,11 +1049,21 @@ vn_queue_submission_init_syncs(struct vn_queue_submission *submit)
       assert(fence->payload->type == VN_SYNC_TYPE_SYNC);
 
       submit->temp.syncs[sync_index] = fence->payload->sync;
-      submit->temp.sync_vals[sync_index] = 1;
+      submit->temp.sync_vals[sync_index++] = 1;
 
       /* fence is backed by renderer sync without renderer object */
       submit->fence_handle = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
    }
+
+   /* The count was taken before vn_queue_submission_init_wait_semaphores
+    * consumed any imported sync fd payloads. A binary semaphore both waited
+    * and signaled in one submission was counted while it still held the
+    * imported payload, but the wait has since restored its permanent one,
+    * which the renderer object signals and which needs no renderer sync.
+    * Submit only what was filled, never a slot nothing wrote.
+    */
+   assert(sync_index <= submit->sync_count);
+   submit->sync_count = sync_index;
 }
 
 static VkResult
